# A note on confidence

Confidence is the line between acting and asking. This walkthrough compresses
that idea into three labels: *confident*, *probable*, and *guess*.
Confident items move to their folder. Probable items move too, but keep a
review marker so you can spot-check. A guess doesn't move at all — it stays
put and becomes a question instead. The threshold between acting and asking
is the whole design. These labels explain the example; they are not a promise
that every Bee Box procedure uses the same names.
